	<h2>24. The Affluent Society</h2>
	<div class="content-content">






<figure class="wp-block-image alignwide size-full"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1000" height="500" src="https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Little_Rock_1958-1000x5001-1.jpg" alt="A young woman sits watching a woman in front of a chalkboard on television." class="wp-image-2150" srcset="https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Little_Rock_1958-1000x5001-1.jpg 1000w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Little_Rock_1958-1000x5001-1-300x150.jpg 300w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Little_Rock_1958-1000x5001-1-768x384.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Little Rock schools closed rather than allow integration. This 1958 photograph shows an African American high school girl watching school lessons on television. Library of Congress (LC-U9- 1525F-28).</figcaption></figure>







